        if ($n % $i == 0) {
            return false;
        }
    }

    return true;
}
```

In this erroneous code, it incorrectly checks for prime numbers using a for loop up to the square root of the number. However, it fails to handle edge cases like negative numbers and non-integer inputs. Also, it uses the `sqrt()` built-in function, which violates the requirement of not using any built-in PHP functions for prime number checking.

