Bitwise operations are used to calculate the maximum value because they allow us to manipulate individual bits of a binary representation of a number. In this case, we left shift 1 by 31 positions to set the sign bit to 1, and then negate the result using the bitwise NOT operator (~). This will give us the maximum positive value that can be stored in an int.

