Here is a Java program that sorts a given list of numbers in descending order using the bubble sort algorithm and bitwise operations for swapping elements:

```java
public class BubbleSortDescending {

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] unsortedList = {7, 6, 5, 4, 3, 2, 1};

        bubbleSortDescending(unsortedList);

        System.out.println("Sorted list in descending order:");
        for (int num : unsortedList) {
            System.out.print(num + " ");
        }
    }

    public static void bubbleSortDescending(int[] arr) {
        int n = arr.length;
        boolean swapped;

        for (int i = 0; i < n - 1; i++) {
            swapped = false;

            for (int j = 0; j < n - i - 1; j++) {
                if (arr[j] < arr[j + 1]) {
                    // Swap the elements using bitwise XOR operation
                    arr[j] = arr[j] ^ arr[j + 1];
                    arr[j + 1] = arr[j] ^ arr[j + 1];
                    arr[j] = arr[j] ^ arr[j + 1];
                    swapped = true;
                }
            }

            // If no swaps occurred in the inner loop, the array is already sorted
            if (!swapped) {
                break;
            }
        }
    }
}
```

