The `find_primes` function first validates the input to ensure it's a positive integer greater than 1. Then, it iterates from 2 up to `n-1` and checks if each number is prime using the `is_prime` function. If it is prime, the number is added to the `primes` list. Finally, the list of prime numbers is returned.

The time complexity of this solution is O(n^1.5) because the `is_prime` function has a time complexity of O(sqrt(n)), and it is called for each number in the range 2 to `n-1`. The space complexity is O(n) because the `primes` list can potentially contain all prime numbers less than `n`.

