```java
import java.util.Scanner;

public class MultiplesOfPrimeNumber {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);
        System.out.print("Enter a number: ");
        int number = scanner.nextInt();

        int count = 0;
        int i = 1;

        // Check if the number is prime
        boolean isPrime = true;
        for (int j = 2; j <= Math.sqrt(number); j++) {
            if (number % j == 0) {
                isPrime = false;
                break;
            }
        }

        // Print the first 15 multiples if number is prime and divisible by 3 and 5
        if (isPrime && number % 3 == 0 && number % 5 == 0) {
            System.out.println("The first 15 multiples of " + number + " that are divisible by both 3 and 5 are:");
            while (count < 15) {
                int multiple = number * i;
                if (multiple % 3 == 0 && multiple % 5 == 0) {
                    System.out.println(multiple);
                    count++;
                }
                i++;
            }
        } else {
            System.out.println("The number is not prime or not divisible by both 3 and 5.");
        }
    }
}
```

In this code, the user is prompted to enter a number. The code checks if the number is prime by iterating from 2 to the square root of the number and checking for any factors. If the number is prime and also divisible by both 3 and 5, it prints the first 15 multiples of the number that are also divisible by 3 and 5. If the number is not prime or not divisible by both 3 and 5, it displays an appropriate message.

