Here's a PHP function that calculates the weighted average of an array of numbers, considering the corresponding weights:

```php
function calculateWeightedAverage($numbers, $weights) {
    // Check if the input arrays have equal lengths
    if (count($numbers) != count($weights)) {
        return "Error: Number and weight arrays must have equal lengths.";
    }

    // Check if the input arrays only contain numeric values
    foreach ($numbers as $number) {
        if (!is_numeric($number)) {
            return "Error: Number array must only contain numeric values.";
        }
    }

    foreach ($weights as $weight) {
        if (!is_numeric($weight)) {
            return "Error: Weight array must only contain numeric values.";
        }
    }

    // Calculate the weighted average
    $weightedSum = 0;
    $totalWeight = 0;

    for ($i = 0; $i < count($numbers); $i++) {
        $weightedSum += $numbers[$i] * $weights[$i];
        $totalWeight += $weights[$i];
    }

    return $weightedSum / $totalWeight;
}
```

