def calculate_average_score(scores):
    if len(scores) < 4:
        return round(sum(scores) / len(scores))

    scores.sort()
    return round(sum(scores[1:-1]) / (len(scores) - 2))
```
The `calculate_average_score` function first checks if the length of the scores list is less than 4. If so, it calculates the average of all scores and returns the rounded result. Otherwise, it sorts the scores list, excludes the first and last elements (highest and lowest scores), calculates the sum of the remaining scores, and returns the rounded average after excluding the highest and lowest scores.

def filter_by(lst, criteria):
    """This function takes an array of elements and a criteria and returns an array of elements filtered by the criteria."""
    return [x for x in lst if criteria(x)]

